        "original_id": "0f55bcd7-0eb7-599c-9a9a-0a72d621e05f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Methodism, Church of England\n- People: John Wesley, Charles Wesley, George Whitefield, Edward Perronet\n- Roles: Anglican cleric, theologian, Anglican priest\n- Events: 18th-century evangelical revival\n\nFacts:\n- In the 18th century, Methodism originated as a revival within the Church of England.\n- John Wesley was born on 28 June 1703 Old Style 17 June 1703 and was an English Anglican cleric and theologian.\n- John Wesley, his brother Charles Wesley, and fellow cleric George Whitefield founded Methodism.\n- Edward Perronet was born in 1726 as the son of an Anglican priest.\n- Edward Perronet worked closely with Anglican priest John Wesley and Charles Wesley for many years during England's eighteenth-century revival.\n- John Wesley died on 2 March 1791.\n- After John Wesley's death, Methodism became a separate denomination.\n- Edward Perronet died on 2 January 1792.",
